    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it sounds like you're saying that \"traditional values\" are basically a problem for democracy. so if i'm writing this blog, should i just frame the debate as \"empathy and inclusivity vs. division and marginalization\"? it seems like there's not really a valid way to argue for tradition in a modern democracy without being \"wrong.\"",
